Y3ti Audits — Raptoreum SmartNode Package
=========================================

THIS REPOSITORY AND ITS RELEASE ARTIFACTS CONTAIN TWO SEPARATE BODIES OF WORK UNDER
TWO DIFFERENT LICENCES. Read both before using, copying or distributing anything here.

THE CURRENT VERSION OF THIS FILE IS PUBLISHED AT
https://github.com/SerpentXSF/rtm-testnet-with-Y3ti-Audits
and the copy in your archive may be older than it. The permissions in section 1 only ever
WIDEN (see the end of that section), so where the two differ, the published version is the
one you may rely on. This pointer exists because earlier archives shipped a narrower licence
with nothing in them to say where the authoritative text lived.


1. THE Y3ti AUDITS SOFTWARE  —  proprietary, all rights reserved
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Copyright (c) 2026 SerpentXSF (Y3ti Audits). All rights reserved.

Covers everything authored for Y3ti Audits, including but not limited to the node
agent, the hardened scan sandbox and its scanner adapters, the control panel, the
packaging and build scripts, and the accompanying documentation. In the release
archives this is the `y3ti/` directory, and the whole of the
`y3ti-audits-testnet-node` package.

YOU ARE PERMITTED TO:

  a) download, install, run and operate this software for the purpose of operating a
     Y3ti Audits validator node on the Raptoreum network, including on hardware you
     control and for as many of your own nodes as you wish;

  b) read, inspect and audit the source, and reproduce the builds, in order to verify
     what you are running — this software asks you to trust consensus results, and you
     are entitled to check it;

  c) modify your own copy locally where that is necessary to operate, debug, package
     or integrate it on your own systems; and

  d) make backup copies for those purposes; and

  e) redistribute and mirror this software, including handing it to another operator,
     PROVIDED THAT what you pass on is a COMPLETE and UNMODIFIED release archive exactly
     as published, with every copyright, licence and attribution notice intact, and that
     the published `SHA256SUMS.txt` for that release accompanies it or is otherwise
     available to the person receiving it.

     That condition is the point of the permission, not paperwork attached to it. This
     software asks you to trust consensus results, so whoever receives a copy has to be
     able to tell whether what reached them is what was actually released. Checksums they
     can verify make that possible. A modified copy makes it impossible, which is why (f)
     below reserves it.

YOU ARE NOT PERMITTED TO, without prior written permission from the copyright holder:

  f) redistribute, publish or make available a MODIFIED copy of this software, or any
     part of it in isolation -- the permission in (e) covers complete, unmodified
     releases and nothing else;

  g) sublicense, sell, rent, lease or offer it as part of any paid or unpaid service;

  h) use it, in whole or in part, to build or operate a competing code-audit,
     code-scanning or consensus-verification service; or

  i) remove, obscure or alter any copyright, licence or attribution notice.

Permission under (a)-(e) is granted for as long as you comply with this licence, and
ends automatically if you do not.

THIS GRANT SUPERSEDES THE COPIES IN EARLIER ARCHIVES, AND ONLY EVER WIDENS THEM. Release
archives published before this change -- r11 and r12, agents 2.1.33 and 2.1.34 -- ship an
earlier version of this file whose clause (e) forbade redistribution outright. The
copyright holder grants the permission above for those releases too: if you hold an older
archive, you may rely on this version. Nothing here takes away a permission anyone
already had.

NO WARRANTY. THIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS
OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR
