THIS IS A TESTNET RELEASE. Rewards are testnet RTM and have no monetary value. Nothing
here is a representation about mainnet behaviour, availability or rewards.


2. RAPTOREUM CORE AND ITS PREDECESSORS  —  MIT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Raptoreum Core is the work of the Raptoreum, Dash and Bitcoin Core developers and is
licensed under the MIT licence, whose full text is `LICENSE-RAPTOREUM`, distributed
alongside this file. Nothing in section 1 adds to, removes from or otherwise affects your
rights in that software, and nothing in this file claims any copyright over it. Wherever
upstream material is distributed with Y3ti Audits it is the official upstream release,
redistributed verbatim and unmodified.

HOW UPSTREAM REACHES YOU DEPENDS ON WHICH PACKAGE YOU HAVE, so what follows is the rule and
not one package's layout. An earlier version of this paragraph named a single layout -- the
`upstream/` directory together with the `raptoreumd`, `raptoreum-cli` and `raptoreum-tx`
binaries -- and no package has ever had both, so it was wrong about every package it shipped
in. A package may:

  a) carry upstream's compiled binaries, `raptoreumd`, `raptoreum-cli` and `raptoreum-tx`,
     together with the files released beside them;

  b) carry upstream's source release as an archive under `upstream/`, with its SHA-256
     beside it; or

  c) carry no upstream material at all, and instead build a container that downloads one
     specific upstream release. See `raptoreum/docker/Dockerfile`, which pins both the URL
     and the SHA-256 of what it fetches.

Case (c) is why `LICENSE-RAPTOREUM` ships even in a package that contains no upstream code.
The notice has to reach whoever ends up RUNNING the software, and that package is the one
that installs it.


Questions about licensing, or a use not permitted above, go to the copyright holder through
https://github.com/SerpentXSF/rtm-testnet-with-Y3ti-Audits.
